# Ada.

language ada
files *.adb *.ads *.ada *.gpr
ignore-case

comment --
string " doubled

# A tick is three things: a character literal, 'x'; the start of an
# attribute, X'Length; and a qualified expression, T'(...). A name before
# '( is the type being qualified, and its tick is taken with it, so the
# character literal rule never sees '(' there. A character literal is
# tried before an attribute, which is any other tick before a name.
match (?P<type>[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_]*)(?P<punctuation>')\(
match string '.'
match (?P<punctuation>')(?P<function>[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_]*)

# A based literal, 16#FF# or 2#1010_1010#, and a decimal one with
# underscores and an exponent: 1_000, 3.14, 1.0E-6.
numbers [0-9][0-9_]*#[0-9A-Fa-f_]+(?:\.[0-9A-Fa-f_]+)?#(?:[eE][-+]?[0-9][0-9_]*)?|[0-9][0-9_]*(?:\.[0-9][0-9_]*)?(?:[eE][-+]?[0-9][0-9_]*)?

keywords abort abs abstract accept access aliased all and array at begin body
keywords case constant declare delay delta digits do else elsif end entry
keywords exception exit for function generic goto if in interface is limited
keywords loop mod new not of or others out overriding package parallel pragma
keywords private procedure protected raise range record rem renames requeue
keywords return reverse select separate some subtype synchronized tagged task
keywords terminate then type until use when while with xor

types Boolean Character Wide_Character Wide_Wide_Character Integer Natural
types Positive Short_Integer Long_Integer Long_Long_Integer Float Short_Float
types Long_Float Long_Long_Float String Wide_String Wide_Wide_String Duration
types Unbounded_String Address

constants True False null

declares function function procedure entry
declares type type subtype package task protected
